# No AI Co-authored-by

Never attribute git commits, PRs, or merge messages to Cursor or any AI agent.

## Commits

- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any AI/agent variant).
- Do **not** pass `--trailer "Co-authored-by: …"` when running `git commit`.
- The author of record is the human who reviewed and merged.

## Pull requests

- Do **not** include `Co-authored-by` lines for AI agents in PR titles, bodies, or squash-merge messages.

## When committing on behalf of the user

Use a plain commit only:

```bash
git commit -m "type(scope): summary"
```

Human co-authors are fine when the user explicitly requests them. AI/agent co-authors are never allowed.
